0	120	Meglena Shtilianova Kuneva (Bulgarian: Меглена Щилиянова Кунева; born 22 June 1957) is a Bulgarian and EU politician.



120	229	Early life and education
Born in Sofia, Kuneva is descended from a Catholic family from the town of Rakovski.
230	321	She graduated in Law from Sofia University in 1981, and in 1984 she became a Doctor of Law.
322	460	She worked as a journalist for the Law Programme of the Bulgarian National Radio while being an assistant professor at Sofia University.  
460	630	As an anchor, she participated in various campaigns related ti human rights, such as the abolition of the death penalty, which still existed at that time in the country.

630	728	In 1990 she took a job as Senior Legal Advisor at the Council of Ministers and held it until 2001.
729	862	In the meantime Kuneva specialized in Foreign Affairs and Environmental Law at Georgetown University and the University of Oxford.



862	1060	Political career


